---
const steps = [
  ['01', 'Learn the operation', 'Understand the people, constraints, data, and decisions behind the visible task. Most of the edge is in what the operation already knows and has not written down.'],
  ['02', 'Find the public record', 'Parcels, deeds, filings, permits, registries. Locate the source of truth, route around the vendor portal, and confirm the field actually holds what its name claims.'],
  ['03', 'Build the system', 'Directed AI agents for implementation, Python for the pipeline, Git for the audit trail. Every route, join, and owner field gets re-verified by hand before it is trusted.'],
  ['04', 'Publish with limits', 'State the finding, the method, and what was not checked.'],
];
---

<section id="method" class="border-y border-rule bg-paper-deep/35 py-14 md:py-20">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="atlas-rule"><span>Working method</span></div>
    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 md:grid-cols-[1fr_2fr] md:gap-14">
      <div>
        <h2 class="display text-3xl md:text-4xl">Opportunity, then evidence.</h2>
        <p class="copy mt-4 max-w-sm text-sm md:text-base">
          The same four moves whether the object is a close process, a county assessor's
          endpoint, or a public company's facility list.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {steps.map(([number, title, body]) => (
          <li class="border-t border-rule py-5">
            <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
              <span class="plate-roman text-sm">{number}</span>
              <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">{title}</p>
            </div>
            <p class="copy mt-2 text-sm">{body}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
